                      "id": "rLiMP",
                      "name": "cmp/GlyphIcon · Status",
                      "context": "Linear-style state ring. Reads run lifecycle as a filling circle before the label: Draft (dashed ring) → Queued (open ring) → Running (half pie) → Needs review (three-quarter pie) → Passed (filled + check) → Cancelled (filled + x). Driven entirely by the `ring` theme axis; colour comes from $ds-state-* so it re-themes with mode.\n\nBuilt from four mutually exclusive marks toggled by boolean tokens — Ring (open, $ring-solid), Disc (filled, $ring-filled), Dash 1-8 ($ring-dash), plus Pie ($ring-pie) and Glyph ($ring-glyph) on top. innerRadius is LITERAL on purpose: binding a number variable to innerRadius resolves wrong (0.76 comes back as 0.0076, collapsing the ring into a solid disc), so do not re-introduce $ring-inner.\n\nFixed 16x16 — children are absolutely positioned, so overriding the root size will not scale them. Intended as the leading icon inside cmp/SessionIndicator.",
                      "theme": {
                        "ring": "progress"
                      },
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 16,
                      "height": 16,
                      "layout": "none",
                      "children": [
