            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "fpobM",
              "name": "Chat & sessions · Component masters",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wLSbp",
                  "name": "Section Title",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg",
                  "content": "Chat & sessions",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "XuPWT",
                  "name": "Browse masters",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "gap": 20,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "qF9a4",
                      "name": "cmp/ConversationBrowse · Tick",
                      "context": "One tick = one user message, in conversation order.\n\nLength is NOT data — it is proximity to the pointer. At rest every tick is the same 10; as the pointer moves down the rail each tick grows toward 26 on a raised-cosine falloff over 4 neighbours, so the rail reads as a lens tracking the cursor. Ticks grow along X only: their y never moves, so the row you are aiming at cannot slip out from under you while the lens swells.\n\nHeight $tick-h (2), radius 1. tick axis: default (fg.subtle, at rest or outside the lens) | hover (fg.muted, inside the lens) | active (fg, the tick under the pointer — the one the ChatBrowseCard is showing). Colour and length fall off together. Everything returns to default/10 when the pointer leaves the rail.",
                      "theme": {
                        "tick": "default"
                      },
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 18,
                      "height": 2,
                      "fill": "$tick-fill",
                      "cornerRadius": 1
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "O4EJB2",
                      "name": "cmp/ConversationBrowse · Card",
                      "context": "Hover preview for a ChatBrowse tick. Shows the turn the tick indexes: the user Message (fg, the thing you are aiming for) over a muted Reply preview that identifies which turn it was — the message alone is often not enough to tell two similar asks apart.\n\nBoth lines are clamped to 2 lines and ellipsized; the card is a fixed 320 so the rail does not jitter as you move down it. Opens on hover of a tick and follows that tick's y, clamped inside the panel. Reply is optional — hide it for a turn the agent has not answered yet.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 320,
                      "fill": "$ds-elevated",
                      "cornerRadius": 10,
                      "stroke": "$ds-border",
                      "strokeWidth": 1,
                      "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 7,
                      "padding": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "TrZkC",
                          "name": "Message",
                          "fill": "$ds-fg",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "all fields are empty in the dashboard, no metric…",
                          "lineHeight": 1.45,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                          "fontSize": 13,
                          "fontWeight": "500"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "QqgJO",
                          "name": "Reply",
                          "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "I found the mismatch: Settings contained alice-token, while this relaunched fixture expects local-dev. After saving the correct token, the…",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                          "fontSize": 12,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "As8PG",
                      "name": "cmp/ConversationBrowse",
                      "context": "ChatBrowse — the conversation scrubber in the ChatPanel's left gutter. One tick per user message, in order, so a long session becomes something you can scan and jump through instead of scrolling. It is the only navigation the turn log has. It indexes the whole conversation, not the visible fragment, so the tick count does not change as the log scrolls.\n\nThe rail is a lens, not a chart: tick length encodes distance from the pointer, never message content. At rest it is a uniform 10-wide ladder; the ticks nearest the cursor swell toward 26 (raised-cosine over 4 neighbours), which makes a 2px target tractable without moving it — growth is along X only, so no tick ever changes y. The tick under the pointer is tick='active' and raises cmp/ConversationBrowseCard with that turn; clicking scrolls the log to that message. The rail is pinned to the viewport, centred vertically — it does not scroll with the log.\n\nTwo modes, by container width:\n• ≥480 — gutter. In-flow beside the turn log, width 40 (px 7, so a 26px tick clears exactly), gap 7. It reserves its own space and can never cover a message. The empty gutter right of a resting tick is the room the lens needs; do not shrink the frame to the ink, it IS the hit target.\n• <480 — floating. A 40px gutter is affordable in a full view and not in a sidebar, so the rail stops reserving space and overlays the log's left edge: the messages keep the full width and gain no padding. It fades in on pointer proximity rather than sitting there permanently.\n\nSCRIM (floating only): the rail is the one thing here that covers content, so it needs a background — but that background must be the surface it covers. $rail-float-fill is the panel's own bg at full alpha, held to 55% of the width and then fading to $rail-float-fade. Do NOT reach for bg.subtle or an elevated tone: anything lighter than the panel stops reading as the panel showing through and becomes a grey chip pinned to the messages. Skip Pencil's background_blur — it previews as a light frosted plate and misrepresents the colour.\n\nBALANCE: in gutter mode the rail is an inset, not a margin — mirror it. The log gets an equal 40 on the right, and the composer takes the same inset on both sides, so the turn log and the input area share one column (panel padding 16 + 40 = 56 a side) and the conversation stays centred. A rail that pads only the left is the bug this rule exists to prevent. Floating mode needs no mirror: it reserves nothing, which is the whole point.\n\nNever place the rail beside the composer in either mode. Hide it below ~3 user messages, where it costs a gutter and buys nothing.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 40,
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 7,
                      "padding": [
                        10,
                        7
                      ],
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "c0UiQ",
                          "type": "ref",
                          "ref": "qF9a4",
                          "name": "Tick 1",
                          "width": 10,
                          "theme": {
                            "tick": "default"
                          }
                        },
                        {
