                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "mdq7n",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatToolDiff",
                      "context": "An expanded patch: the collapsed row plus the hunk it wrote. The diff IS the artifact — a patch reported only as '+1 -1' asks you to take the agent's word for it, and this is the one tool whose result you most want to read.\n\nSame block shell as cmp/ChatToolTimeline: one labelled surface, no Input/Output split. The label is the file; the counts sit opposite it, so the header answers 'what changed and how much' before you read a line.\n\nLines are full-bleed — the tint runs the whole block width, not just behind the glyph — and mono, unwrapped, clipped at the edge. Only -/+ lines are tinted; context lines stay bare so the eye lands on the change. Show the hunk, not the file: a few lines of context either side is the point, and anything longer belongs behind a 'view file' affordance.",
