                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "TDV8W",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatInput",
                      "context": "ChatInput (@pstdio/ui). Editor above one toolbar row; attachments are optional. All composer controls and mode tags are 28px high. Root padding and gap are 8px. Toolbar: Attach, model parameter controls, optional closable mode tags, spacer, Send. Attach and parameter buttons use ghost styling. Send uses the implemented primary IconButton with a 16px arrow or filled pause. Mode tags use the shared subtle ticket tag pill styling at 28px. Send swaps arrow-up for pause while streaming. Preserve disabled control styling. Model selection uses the shared SelectorTrigger with ghost styling; the harness belongs in its menu header. Mode tags sit immediately right of all model parameters and use cmp/ComposerModeTag. Selecting /goal at the caret removes only the slash fragment and keeps the objective text. Close removes a draft intent or requests native clear/leave for a submitted mode. Keep the draft and retain native state until acknowledgement. Submitted goal tags keep the objective visible; details and actions depend on provider capabilities. Multiple new intents require verified composition. Use the shared Menu surface with icon-free SearchableMenuItem rows for slash completion. Do not show mode status cards or argument dialogs.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "fill": "$ds-bg",
                      "cornerRadius": 4,
